WEBVTT

00:00:00.016 --> 00:00:05.952
Partition pruning means Spark can skip reading some partitions when a filter matches the partition layout.

00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:10.502
A date column can be useful if queries often filter by date range.

00:00:10.502 --> 00:00:16.432
A unique ID is usually a poor partition column because it can create many tiny partitions.

00:00:16.432 --> 00:00:19.722
Partition design should follow query patterns.

00:00:19.722 --> 00:00:25.772
Partitions organize data so the engine can avoid reading files that cannot satisfy a filter.

00:00:25.772 --> 00:00:30.952
Good partition columns are commonly filtered and have manageable cardinality.

00:00:30.952 --> 00:00:35.047
Column pruning similarly avoids reading unused columns.

00:00:35.047 --> 00:00:39.520
Both optimizations reduce I/O before more expensive computation begins.
